WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:04.770
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.
I found this neat puzzle on the Internet.

00:00:06.129 --> 00:00:08.459
Imagine a rectangular grid of circles.

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:14.740
We'll color in some of the circles with blue dots to make a mathematical equation.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:25.320
It currently reads (71 + 1)(71 − 1) = 71.

00:00:26.260 --> 00:00:28.760
But this is not a correct equation.

00:00:29.980 --> 00:00:33.880
The puzzle is to either color one blue dot,

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:38.180
or erase one blue dot to make a valid equation.

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:41.400
Can you figure it out?

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:46.980
Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for a solution.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.200
So, how can we make this a valid equation?

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:10.880
The surprising answer is that in the very last digit of 1,

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:14.080
erase the second blue dot from the bottom.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.560
The left-hand side of this equation

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:30.600
evaluates to (71 + 1)(71 - 1) = 72 × 70 = 5040.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:35.100
The right hand side evaluates to 7 factorial.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.420
The one becomes an exclamation point which is a factorial,

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:45.980
so we take the product of 1 to 7, and we get 5040.

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:48.820
And that's how we get a valid equation.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:51.500
Did you figure it out?

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.680
Thanks for watching this video.

